\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks slip on profit-taking, peso flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2005\par 23:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks slipped on Thursday amid profit-taking a day after shares notched a new high, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of 11 leading stocks dipped 0.39 percent to close at 1,652.38. The index has accumulated a gain of 20 percent so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was a brisk 84.1 million pesos ($28.9 million).  \par \par \uc2 "The fall was foreseeable because the MerVal seemed weary of rising, with many highs and few corrections," said Ruben Pascuali, trader at Mayoral Bursatil brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 "There could be more profit-taking given a slowdown in some economic variables and above all because of the result of yesterday's auction, which shows disinterest in placing bonds at the yields that the government wants," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Argentina offered $800 million in Boden 2015 dollar-denominated bonds on the local market to help finance debt payments later this year, but the average yield on bids was 8.8 percent, a rate the government was unwilling to pay.  \par \par \uc2 MerVal heavyweight Grupo Financiero Galicia was among Thursday's losers, shedding 1.2 percent to end at 2.46 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> closed steady at 2.91/2.9125 per dollar thanks to ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the peso weak for exports.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050922e19m002fs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
