\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Mostly Firm  \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2005\par 22:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso continued to lose ground against the dollar Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid reduced investor dollar inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Locally traded bonds, meanwhile, were mostly firm although the popular restructured discount bond in pesos was down slightly.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.9200, slightly weaker than ARS2.9175 on Monday, and down from ARS2.905 at Thursday's close. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday night released a new banking rule that has slowed the inflow of dollars into the market by requiring foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tagged for exporter pre-financing to be lined up with actual shipments.  \par \par \uc2 "The bank believed that speculative capital was coming in under the guise of export pre-financing" to avoid capital controls set in place earlier this year, said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Hector Blanco of local ABC Mercado de Cambio. "Once in, these dollars were used to buy pesos to buy bonds and other investments."  \par \par \uc2 As such, traders "expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to easily sustain the exchange rate for at least the next two weeks due to the lack of dollars," Blanco said. [ 13-09-05 2017GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, bonds were mostly firm, said Alejandro Barros, a financial analyst with local Banco Piano.  \par \par \uc2 Among peso notes, the newly restructured discount was at ARS121.20, down slightly from ARS122.70, while the par was at ARS47.85 from ARS47.90 and the Bogar 2018 was at ARS144.80 from ARS144.60.  \par \par \uc2 Among dollar-denominated notes, the par under Argentine law was at ARS100.80 from ARS100.75, while the Argentine jurisdiction discount bond was at ARS290.00 from ARS291.00.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 13-09-05 2029GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050913e19d000xt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
