\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Firm  \b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.    \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Sep 09, 2005 (ODC via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 (Recasts to update with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data)  \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso retreated Friday as continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aimed at weakening the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , got a boost from new bank rules for trade finance.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, local bonds remained well bid.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.9125 against the dollar, weaker than Thursday's close at ARS2.9050.  \par \par \uc2 Fernando Izzo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local ABC Mercado de Cambio, said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying was clearly evident through parts of the trading session. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported later that it bought $22 million in the open market Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Izzo expects that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have an easier time maintaining a weaker peso from now on, thanks to a new rule the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  published Thursday night that places tighter controls on exporter financing. The move is expected to close loopholes that some investors had been using to get around Argentine capital controls.  \par \par \uc2 "Now dollars won't be able to happily roll into the stock and bond markets," Izzo said. "The expectation is that there will be less dollars now with this dollar selling restriction."  \par \par \uc2 As such, "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely buy less" dollars on a daily basis to maintain a weaker peso that favors Argentine exports, Izzo said.  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the local bond market was "basically strong," although in weaker volumes from days in which stronger gains have been seen, said Javier Salvucci, an analyst at Silver Cloud Advisors in Buenos Aires.  \par \par \uc2 He said the fact that many bonds had held to their recent gains even though they may have reached the top end of their trading limits is "a good signal" for the market.  \par \par \uc2 Nor did there seem to be any disruption in the market from news that the government is planning to issue another 2015 bond in two weeks. The Boden 2014, one of the most actively traded peso bonds and one with a similar maturity as the planned new bond, rose slightly to ARS99.50 from its close of ARS99.4 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The par bond in pesos, which some Wall Street analysts have been recommending as a beneficiary of declining global interest rates was unchanged at ARS47.2. The discount bond in pesos was also unchanged at ARS123.15.  \par \par \uc2 -By Michael Casey and Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4313 1918; michael.j.casey@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 09-09-05 1752ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050909e199006vu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
