\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks flat,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  reigns in peso  \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2005\par 23:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Sept 7 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks closed unchanged on Wednesday, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a record dollar purchase to keep the peso from appreciating.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark MerVal index <.MERV> of 11 leading stocks ended steady at 1,608.03 points but has racked up gains of 1.67 percent in the first week of September and and 16.92 percent for the year.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume on the Buenos Aires exchange totaled 105.1 million pesos ($36.3 million).  \par \par \uc2 "We saw the MerVal correcting itself today and fighting to close above 1,600 points,"said Leopoldo Olivari of Bacque Sociedad brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 Steelmaker Acindar closed up 2.78 percent to 5.54 pesos while Tenaris slid 1.31 percent to 33.9 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> closed even at 2.89/2.8925 pesos the dollar, steadied by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases as part of the government's efforts to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak and boost exports.  \par \par \uc2 A source who follows the bank's activity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $189.2 million, beating a $172.4 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Aug. 3.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050907e197002bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\