\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens On More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Mixed  \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2005\par 21:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso weakened slightly against the dollar Friday on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and some late-session dollar buying by private banks jittery over a political scandal in Brazil.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, locally traded bonds were mixed as some notes saw a return to the profit taking that has dominated sessions throughout much of the month.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.9100 against the dollar, slightly weaker than Thursday's close at ARS2.9050.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Fernando Izzo with local ABC Mercado de Cambio said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily as the session opened, "but once it saw the market was following it, it stopped buying" dollars.  \par \par \uc2 Izzo suggested that some banks started buying dollars after the real in neighboring Brazil opened weaker partly on worries that it could quickly plummet on new revelations in the political corruption scandal there.  \par \par \uc2 "A few banks wanted to change some pesos into dollars to wait and see what happens" in Brazil, Izzo said. "But it was far from a madhouse; the price of the peso barely changed compared with yesterday."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought $33 million in the open market Friday, down from $53 million a day earlier. [ 26-08-05 1956GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, notes were mixed amid average volume, said Alejandro Barros, a financial analyst with local Banco Piano.  \par \par \uc2 "With some minor exceptions, most bonds were down by between 0.2% and 0.5%," Barros said. Among losers, the restructured discount in pesos was at ARS116.45 by late afternoon, down from ARS116.90 on Thursday, while the Bogar 2018 was down to ARS138.75 from ARS139.60. Both bonds saw mild rebounds during the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 Among the few gainers, the restructured par in pesos was up slightly to ARS43.54 from ARS43.40 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 26-08-05 2007GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050826e18q0011e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
