\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weaker On More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Mixed  \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Continued dollar buying by the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday helped the peso lose more ground against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a government goal aimed at favoring Argentine exports despite increasing inflationary concerns.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, bonds were mixed in a slow session.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.8825 to the dollar, weaker than Thursday's close of ARS2.8775.  \par \par \uc2 As with other recent sessions, "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought as the market opened, marking a price above the previous close," said Hector Blanco, a trader with local brokerage ABC Mercado de Cambio. Several private banks followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lead and sold some dollars, he added.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been busy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market this month to soften the peso. Prior to Friday's session, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought some $850 million since Aug. 1, when the peso was at ARS2.8600 to the dollar, its strongest level in more than a year.  \par \par \uc2 Blanco estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought another $80 to $100 million on Friday, although official data would not be available until later in the day. [ 12-08-05 2005GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The local bond market lacked direction amid low volume, said Alejandro Barros, a financial analyst with local Banco Piano.  \par \par \uc2 "There was very little variation and volume was low. There is some uncertainty about inflation and where the exchange rate is going," Barros said. Investors are also closely following news from Brazil, since any fallout from government corruption allegations there "is going to have an effect here," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Among losers Friday, the restructured discount bond in pesos was down to ARS116.90 from ARS117.20, while the Bocon Pro 11 was down to ARS164.14 from ARS164.73. On the upside, the par in dollars under Argentine jurisdiction was up to ARS94.50 from ARS93.50.  \par \par \uc2 Argentine markets will be closed Monday for a national holiday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 12-08-05 2012GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050812e18c000si\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
