\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Up   \b0\par\par\uc2 451 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.     \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Aug 09, 2005 (ODC via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data)   \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso weakened for the fourth straight session Tuesday on steady \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which Economy Minister Roberto Lavagna told business leaders will remain an important part of the government's economic policy.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, bonds began to recover from a recent bout of profit-taking.   \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.8750 against the dollar, slightly weaker than ARS2.8700 on Monday and weaker than ARS2.8600 on Aug. 3, when record \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying helped hold the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a strong point.   \par \par \uc2 Lavagna told business leaders Tuesday at a conference of the Argentine Industrial Union in Cordoba that the current competitive exchange rate "is not enough, is not a sufficient condition" for sustained growth, "but at the same time without it there is no sustainable growth and social development program. In other words, it is a necessary condition."   \par \par \uc2 Although the peso has strengthened from the ARS3.00 level that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained for some time after the end of the one-to-one "convertibility" peg to the U.S. dollar in January 2002, most economists say they believe the peso is severely undervalued relative to competing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Brazilian real, which has rallied tremendously over the past year.   \par \par \uc2 Daniel Bou Kahir, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at local Banco de la Pampa, said the government will end up paying a price for maintaining a weaker peso.   \par \par \uc2 "It is going to continue to emit pesos, and going to have to pay higher yields to absorb those same pesos. Nothing is free," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Bou Kahir said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was busy buying dollars throughout the day, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported later that it bought $75.7 million during the session.   \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, profit-taking continued into the morning, but quickly fell off in the afternoon as bonds began to recover lost ground, said Noelia Lucini, an analyst at Capital Markets Argentina.   \par \par \uc2 Investors were especially quick to return to the restructured discount bond in pesos, which was last quoted at ARS120.20, up from ARS119.7 on Monday. The restructured par in pesos also was rebounding to ARS45.55 from ARS44.70. Among the few notes still seeing some profit-taking was the Bocon Pro 12, down to ARS168.80 from ARS169.50.   \par \par \uc2 "It looks like the profit-taking is over for now, but the rest of the month should be much more selective than July and June," Lucini said.   \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 08-09-05 1750ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050809e1890073q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
