\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks close slightly up on select buying  \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 22:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, July 22 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks closed a touch higher on Friday in a market showing low volume and selective buying due to strong competition from the bond market, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> of the 11 leading stocks closed 0.18 percent higher at 1,481.79 points, for a 1.3 percent gain during the week. MerVal shares are up 7.7 percent since Jan. 1.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume was a low 68 million pesos ($24 million).  \par \par \uc2 A buoyant bond market, with inflation-indexed paper in high demand, has diverted interest from stocks in recent weeks.  \par \par \uc2 "The market should begin to react, with bank shares leading due to the rise in bond prices," said Hector Bergoglio, trader at Rabello brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 Banco Rio was one of the best performers on Friday, rising 6.4 percent to 2.50 pesos, while Banco Hipotecario lost 2.3 percent to 13.0 pesos on news that it might fail in its attempt to buy the local subsidiary of Banca Nazionale del Lavoro.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> closed steady at 2.865/2.8675 per dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $38 million to stem a further appreciation of the peso, now at 14-month highs.  \par \par \uc2 The peso is 3.75 percent stronger so far this year, but the government wants to keep it weak with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to benefit exports.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050722e17m0024i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
