\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Flat As  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Counters Yuan News  \b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2005\par 21:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso ended Thursday unchanged as heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to offset an early gain on news that China has allowed its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan, to trade against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.8625 to the dollar, unchanged from Wednesday's close. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained to ARS2.8600 during the first hour of trading, but was held there as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to buy dollars. Heavy buying during the last hour managed to push the peso back to end unchanged on the day.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, locally traded bonds were mostly down on some mild profit taking triggered by the revaluation news.  \par \par \uc2 China's decision to scrap the yuan's peg to the dollar will likely make it harder for the Argentine government to target a weaker peso that favors exports, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 On one hand, if a stronger yuan "reduces the inflow of Chinese imports, importers won't have to buy as many dollars to pay for the goods," said trader Daniel Bou Kahir with local Banco de la Pampa. On the other hand, "if we sell more exports to China, more dollars will come in from exporters. That will mean that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to emit more pesos, with the related inflationary concerns," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Prior to the entrance of foreign investors with the conclusion of Argentina's long-awaited debt restructuring this year, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had settled into a routine in which cereal exporters repatriated overseas dollar earnings and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadily bought dollars to maintain a weaker peso that favored exports. The government aimed to hold the peso near a 3-to-1 mark against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But meeting that goal has become increasingly difficult to achieve as foreign investors flood in seeking peso-denominated bonds and other investments. Consequently, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to step up its dollar buying in recent months, only to see the peso reach its strongest point in more than a year. [ 21-07-05 1951GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, inflation is on the rise. Most analysts see it coming in above 10% for the year, higher than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's original 8% ceiling.  \par \par \uc2 Economist Alberto Bernal, with Ideaglobal in New York, said sooner or later Argentine planners will have to accept a stronger peso.  \par \par \uc2 "The Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has two choices: accept this fact or try to block the sun with one hand," Bernal said. "Everybody in the market knows that (the peso will strengthen). That's why they keep buying Argentine peso bonds linked to inflation - because it's a beautiful investment."  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, news of the yuan's revaluation led to some mild profit-taking.  \par \par \uc2 Among sliders, the peso-denominated Bocon Pro 12 was last quoted at ARS161.80, down from ARS163.00, while the Boden 2012, a dollar note, was down to ARS259.00 from ARS259.60.  \par \par \uc2 Noelia Lucini, a fixed-income trader with Capital Markets Argentina, said a stronger yuan "will have a gradual affect" on local bonds.  \par \par \uc2 "Attention is going to focus on U.S. markets, watching to see what happens with the 10-year Treasurys. I think the local market will take advantage of this to make more adjustments," she said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 21-07-05 2005GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050721e17l000zf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
