\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Bonds Hit Lull;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Holds Peso Steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Jul 01, 2005 (ODC via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 Argentine bonds were flat or down slightly Friday on some mild profit taking after a strong month, while heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to hold the peso flat on the day at ARS2.8875.  \par \par \uc2 Paulino Seoane, a fixed income analyst with local Lopez Leon Brokers, said volume was low ahead of the U.S. independence holiday on Monday. "From noon on there was nothing going on; Monday should be even slower," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Friday's session was marked by "some profit taking and arbitrage between long-term and short-term bonds," Seoane added. "Just about everything was down slightly, except for the discount in pesos," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The newly restructured discount bond was last quoted at ARS103.10, unchanged from Thursday's close. Among sliders, the restructured peso-denominated par bond was down to ARS38.75 from ARS39.00, while the pre-debt swap Bocon Pro 12, also in pesos, was down to ARS149.55 from ARS151.60.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was busy buying dollars all day to offset heavy repatriations of overseas dollar earnings by cereal exporters, said Hernan Korin, a local portfolio manager with Supervielle Asset Management.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should curb its heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by mid-July as cereal exporters "liquidate" less overseas earners in the wake of the year's heaviest harvest period, he added.  \par \par \uc2 In addition to heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the government has recently launched a series of measures aimed at sustaining a weaker peso that favors Argentine exports.  \par \par \uc2 Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began requiring importers to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment in which they place an order for foreign-made consumer goods. On Wednesday the Economy Ministry published a resolution that extended a recently imposed 30% lockup on foreign inflows to Argentine residents who bring in more than $2 million a month. Previously, the 30% restriction had applied just to foreigners.  \par \par \uc2 The creative measures have led some economists to believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is obsessed with keeping the exchange rate from rising and is neglecting its primary goal of price stability.  \par \par \uc2 Already, consensus estimates for inflation of 9.8% at year-end suggest the market believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fail to achieve its 5%-to-8% inflation target.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 07-01-05 1619ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050701e1710069c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
