ded.  \par \par \uc2 In addition to heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the government has recently launched a series of measures aimed at sustaining a weaker peso that favors Argentine exports.  \par \par \uc2 Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began requiring importers to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment in which they place an order for foreign-made consumer goods. On Wednesday the Economy Ministry published a resolution that extended a recently imposed 30% lockup on foreign inflows to Argentine residents who bring in more than $2 million a month. Previously, the 30% restriction had applied just to foreigners.  \par \par \uc2 The creative measures have led some economists to believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is obsessed with keeping the exchange rate from rising and is neglecting its primary goal of price stability.  \par \par \uc2 Already, consensus estimates for inflation of 9.8% at year-end suggest the market believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fail to achieve its 5%-to-8% inflation target.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 01-07-05 2019GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050701e171000v3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
