\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weaker On Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2005\par 22:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso slid one centavo Monday on continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while bonds were mixed as the government quoted an upcoming coupon for new restructured discount notes.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.8900 against the dollar, a full centavo weaker than Friday's ARS2.8800 close.  \par \par \uc2 Carlos Lizer, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at local Puente Hermanos attributed the drop to "heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And there is also the new measure from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  involving importers." The measure, issued Thursday, requires importers to move forward purchases of dollars to be used to buy incoming goods. As of Friday, importers must now exchange pesos for dollars on the shipping date.  \par \par \uc2 The peso had gained on the dollar over the past two months on a combination of incoming foreign investment dollars tied to the nation's recently settled debt swap and heavy seasonal dollar selling by cereal exporters repatriating overseas earnings.  \par \par \uc2 But with the government seeking to hold the peso closer to the ARS3.00 mark to benefit Argentine exports, government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  planners began deploying an array of measures aimed at softening the peso.  \par \par \uc2 Last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirement for importers followed an Economy Ministry measure earlier this month that imposes a one-year lockup, in an interest-free account, of 30% of all portfolio inflows.  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, the government quoted its third coupon on newly restructured discount bonds in pesos and dollars to be paid out Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Although the news technically should have pushed prices down, continued heavy buying of discount peso notes meant the bond was virtually unchanged from Friday's close, said fixed-income analyst Adolfo Zuberbuhler at local Banco Finansur.  \par \par \uc2 "The price is the same as Friday's close, so the coupon was absorbed in the price," he said. "The discount in dollars was also quoted, but didn't see as much volume. The rest of the bonds were firm, but saw little volume."  \par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated discount bond was last quoted at ARS101.10, unchanged from Friday's close, while the discount in dollars slid on the coupon quote to ARS260.00 from ARS268.00.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 27-06-05 2039GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1833  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050627e16r000v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
