\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Ctrl Bank Issues Record ARS2.248B In Notes  \b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2005\par 01:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a record 2.248 billion pesos ($1=ARS2.894) in Lebac and Nobac notes in its weekly auction, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement released late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it offered ARS800 million in notes and received a record ARS2.484 billion in bids. Ultimately, ARS2.248 billion in bids were accepted, the largest issuance since the Lebac program began three years ago.  \par \par \uc2 Since there were no Lebac and Nobac obligations coming due this week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net absorption was ARS2.248 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses its weekly Lebac auctions, as well as the repurchase securities market, to manage the money supply and offset its dollar-buying in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a record $152.5 million on Friday of last week, its highest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level since \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial crisis of 2002. Dollar purchases were also historically high for much of May, though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's large absorptions muted the effect of the steady stream of pesos being injected into the system.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wailin Wong, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3125; wailin.wong@dowjones.com [ 07-06-05 2336GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050607e16700106\par }\page {