\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Argentina Bonds Fall After Recent Gains;Peso Flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, May 18, 2005 (ODC via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Updates with price for the newly issued Boden 2014 bond and figures on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .)\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's local debt market succumbed to light profit-taking Wednesday, giving up some of its gains from a favorable U.S. court ruling that effectively cleared the government to complete its $103 billion debt restructuring.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Argentine peso closed local trading flat at ARS2.885 to the dollar despite continued strong dollar buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Local bonds had risen strongly after a U.S. federal appeals court overturned Friday an embargo on $7 billion in defaulted Argentine bonds. With this roadblock eliminated, the government should now be able to settle its delayed debt swap. Investors took profits on recent sessions' gains on Wednesday, with most of the actively traded notes falling back.  \par \par \uc2 The Boden 2008 was quoted in late-afternoon trading at ARS115.63, down from Tuesday's close of ARS116.4. The Bocon Pro 12 was at ARS148.35, down from ARS149.8. Bucking the trend was the benchmark dollar-denominated Boden 2012, which was at ARS251, up from ARS250.25.  \par \par \uc2 Analyst Javier Salvucci of Silver Cloud Advisors said there is little consensus over when the new securities under the debt restructuring will be delivered, and the lack of clarity is lending some caution to local fixed-income trading. Salvucci said some market players were speaking of a July settlement date, while others still see the new bonds arriving much sooner - possibly within weeks.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't know if there's worry," Salvucci said. "The fairer word would be caution because the worry was placed over whether the debt swap would be freed. This issue is now closed and the market is a little more positive."  \par \par \uc2 The Bocon Pro 13, a peso-denominated note that Salvucci said is most similar to the upcoming discount bond to be issued under the restructuring, was quoted at ARS61, down slightly from ARS61.5. Salvucci said the Bocon Pro 13 rose nearly 7% in the sessions after the Friday court ruling in the U.S. and is the best barometer of how the new debt will behave when secondary trading in the new bonds begins.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the Boden 2014 was quoted at ARS81.30. It was the first session of trading for the ARS1 billion in Boden 2014 bonds that the government auctioned earlier this month. This was the reopening of an old issue but the first time that Argentina's Treasury had voluntarily placed debt since February 2001. The Boden 2014 bonds had priced at ARS78.7 when they were issued.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, analysts say the anticipated arrival of the new bonds under the restructuring hasn't yet been felt in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which this week has been focused on exporter-related inflows and peso-buying from companies that have large income tax payments due.  \par \par \uc2 "There are huge tax collections this month," said trader Daniel Bou Kahir of Banco de la Pampa. "For that reason, (dollar) selling has accelerated and this has produced a small revaluation of the Argentine peso."  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to ARS2.885 on Monday and hasn't budged from that level, despite aggressive dollar-buying from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and state-owned Banco de la Nacion. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a high $99.5 million during Wednesday's session.  \par \par \uc2 Bou Kahir noted that the pesos streaming in from tax payments go into the accounts of the national tax agency held at Banco Nacion. The state-owned bank in turn uses that money to buy dollars or participate in the securities repurchase, or repo, market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses the repo market, as well as weekly auctions of Lebac notes, to absorb excess liquidity and offset its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a record ARS1.898 billion in Lebac and longer-dated Nobac notes. Over the last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also absorbed ARS2.818 billion through repo transactions. The combined effect of these absorptions has fully compensated for the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's more active dollar-buying in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Since May 10, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought a total $547.1 million. This exceeds its dollar purchases for the entire month of April.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wailin Wong, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3125; wailin.wong@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 05-18-05 1811ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050518e15i002ng\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
