\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Central Bk Absorption Mutes  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2005\par 17:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued ARS1.898 billion ($1=ARS2.885) in Lebac notes Tuesday, a record placement that is helping to offset the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's historically high \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last week.  \par \par \uc2 According to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered a total of ARS1.2 billion in Lebac and longer-dated Nobac notes to roll over ARS1.397 billion coming due this week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  received ARS2.099 billion in bids and ultimately accepted ARS1.898 billion, widening its original offer and absorbing a net ARS501 million. Roberto Drimer, a fixed-income analyst at local consultancy Argentine Research, said the ARS1.898 billion placement is the largest since the Lebac program began in 2002.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses its weekly Lebac auctions, as well as the repurchase securities market, to soak up excess liquidity and manage the money supply. These absorptions offset the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has turned sharply upward in recent sessions.  \par \par \uc2 Over the last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hit its highest daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels of the year, buying $101.5 million during Monday's session alone - its largest daily purchase in nearly two years. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $447.6 million in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since May 10. In April, total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was $473 million.  \par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's record absorptions have muted the effect of the historically high quantity of pesos being put into the system. In addition to the ARS501 million soaked up Tuesday in the weekly Lebac auction, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also absorbed a significant amount - some ARS2.818 billion - through repurchase securities transactions over the last week. As a result, the monetary system has seen net absorption over the last week of about ARS2.021 billion.  \par \par \uc2 "With yesterday's successful Lebac placement, the fear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't comply with its monetary program is substantially reduced," analysts from FyE Consult wrote in a Wednesday report, noting that interest rates for the various Lebac series rose less than expected.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was aggressively expanding monetary supply at the end of 2004, has a contractionary policy for 2005. Faced with a surprise resurgence in inflation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying significantly dwindled in the first quarter of the year.  \par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still seen aligned with the administration's desire to see a "pro-competitive" exchange rate between ARS2.90 and ARS3.00 to the dollar. Because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's newly aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  haven't led to a net injection of pesos into the system, its dollar purchases could be seen as more of an effort to manage the exchange rate than to comply with money supply goals.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, says it buys dollars to balance against the exporter-related inflows that generally dominate local foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. Drimer of Argentine Research said exporter repatriations should drop off in the second half of the year.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wailin Wong, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3125; wailin.wong@dowjones.com [ 18-05-05 1546GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050518e15i000u3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
