\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks dip after big gain on debt ruling  \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2005\par 23:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, May 17 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks retreated slightly on Tuesday after posting hefty gains in the wake of a U.S. court decision to lift a freeze on Argentine bonds and clear the way for the country's debt swap, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The MerVal index <.MERV> finished 0.92 percent lower at 1444.73 points, trimming the gain so far this month to 7.1 percent. Volume fell to 62.5 million pesos ($21.6 million) from a high 91 million pesos on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "The MerVal took a reasonable breather, taking into account that the decline happened with low volume. This is not worrisome profit-taking," said Francisco Marra of Bull Markets Brokers.  \par \par \uc2 A U.S. federal appeals court in New York on Friday lifted an embargo by holdout creditors on $7 billion in Argentine bonds involved in the debt swap, originally scheduled for April 1.  \par \par \uc2 The government could offer this week the new bonds to creditors who accepted the swap terms, allowing Argentina to complete the biggest sovereign restructuring in modern times.  \par \par \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia , which accounts for 25 percent of the index, fell 0.83 percent to 2.38 pesos, while steelmaker Acindar dropped 1.88 percent to 6.25 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso <ARSB=> closed 0.09 percent weaker at 2.89/2.895 per dollar thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soak up high dollar liquidity.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  is awash in dollars thanks to its current soy harvest, the biggest export earner, and good sentiment after the U.S. court decision that opened the way for the debt swap. 