\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weaker On More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Mixed  \b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2005\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso weakened slightly Wednesday on continued heavy dollar buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leading some fixed-income analysts to predict that more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will indirectly push down bond prices.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.8975 to the dollar, slightly weaker than ARS2.8925 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, bonds were mixed amid low volume as investors continue to wait for a U.S. appeals court to rule on a distressed debt holdout case involving the embargo of $7 billion in defaulted bonds tendered in Argentina's restructuring.  \par \par \uc2 In the past week, increased \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying has pumped more than 1 billion pesos into the financial system. The increased buying has led many analysts to believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to raise interest rates more aggressively to reabsorb the new bills and avoid an inflationary impact.  \par \par \uc2 But rising interest rates would undermine local bond prices, said Juan Ignacio Gomez Vega, a fixed income analyst with local InvertirOnline.  \par \par \uc2 Beyond the debt swap settlement, which has been held up by the U.S. lawsuit, "the rest of the year will depend on how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tries to manipulate the money supply," Gomez Vega said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has three objectives at once: a weak peso, low interest rates, and low inflation. That doesn't happen anywhere in the world, yet here we are trying," he said. "We'll have to see how this soap opera develops. When interest rates start going up, bonds will go down."  \par \par \uc2 Among losers Wednesday, the dollar-denominated Boden 2012 was last quoted at ARS245.5, down from ARS246.25 in moderate volume, Gomez Vega said. Among peso-denominated gainers, the Boden 2008 was at 114.9, up from 114.7, while the Bocon Pro 12 rose to ARS143.9 from ARS143.6.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was busy buying dollars all day," said Hector Blanco, a trader with ABC Mercado de Cambio. "There was a rush of heavy dollar buying in the last 10 minutes of the session that looked like it probably came from (state-run) Banco de la Nacion."  \par \par \uc2 Banco de la Nacion, the Treasury's banker, is not required to publish its daily buying data, although traders suspect it has stepped up dollar purchases this year to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to announce its dollar buying later in the day. On Tuesday it bought $79.5 million after buying at least $85 million in the previous three sessions.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying offsets dollar selling by cereal exporters seeking to repatriate overseas earnings. Cereal exporter repatriations are expected to hit their peak this month and next as the year's main harvest wraps up.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 11-05-05 2032GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050511e15b0014q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
