\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens Again On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Down  \b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 20:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso slid for the second straight session Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to step up dollar buying to take advantage of a lull as investors wait for official debt swap results, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The peso lost a centavo against the dollar on the day to close at ARS2.95.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, local bonds issued after Argentina's December 2001 default slipped slightly across the board on low volume.  \par \par \uc2 Many observers expect the peso to see a strong rally on an inflow of foreign investment dollars if the $103 billion debt swap is deemed a success. Initial indications suggest that the swap was well received and the government plans to release preliminary data about its acceptance rate Thursday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Daniel Bou-Khair of local Banco de la Pampa said foreign investors are "still waiting for confirmation" and didn't begin buying pesos in large amounts Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 As such, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  "is being more aggressive this week - taking advantage of an opportunity to weaken the peso," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders see the government trying to hold the peso near a three-to-one ratio against the dollar to give Argentine exports a competitive advantage. Additionally, the government has calculated its budget this year using that exchange rate, they add.  \par \par \uc2 Addressing the legislature Tuesday morning, President Nestor Kirchner appeared to affirm such speculation, saying that a "realistic exchange rate is fundamental," adding that the value of the peso needs to be "pro-production, pro-national employment." [ 01-03-05 1949GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, post-default bonds lost some ground in a quiet session. Volume in locally traded debt has fallen off sharply since Friday's close of the debt swap offering put an end to the market for defaulted notes.  \par \par \uc2 In afternoon trading, the benchmark dollar-denominated Boden 2012 was quoted at ARS257.5 compared with ARS260.5 a day earlier, while the peso-denominated Boden 2008 was off a peso at ARS113.2.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, traders are waiting for the emergence of a gray, or "when and if," market for the new bonds, which are slated for issue on April 1.  \par \par \uc2 "Right now there is only limited activity," said fixed income analyst Mariana de Mendiburu of local Silver Cloud Advisors. "Many investors, especially institutional investors, are waiting for March 18," when the official final results are expected.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 01-03-05 2021GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050301e1310010a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
