\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Dn On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Debt Mixed After Swap  \b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2005\par 20:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso's expected rally following the nation's apparently successful debt swap didn't kick off Monday, as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid slightly against the dollar on late \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by state-run Banco de la Nacion.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, local bonds issued after the nation's December 2001 sovereign debt default were generally up with a few losers on the day, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The peso traded in high volume to close at ARS2.94 against the dollar, slightly weaker than Friday's ARS2.9375.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Jose Nogueira with local ABC Mercado de Cambio attributed the slide to a late-day dollar purchase by Banco de la Nacion. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  offset the peso's gains earlier in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought dollars, though at relatively low levels due to daily limits it has set up to meet tighter first quarter monetary policy goals, Nogueira added.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the peso to surge amid an inflow of foreign investment dollars if Argentina's $103 billion debt swap is deemed a success - thereby releasing the nation from its international financial pariah status.  \par \par \uc2 The bond swap offering closed Friday and initial indications suggest that it will come off successfully, although government officials say that initial results won't be available until Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 However, Nogueira noted that the peso usually weakens at the end of the month as investors seek to buy dollars to close out short positions at the month's end.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the peso will start to strengthen tomorrow (Tuesday), with the beginning of a new month," he said. [ 28-02-05 1953GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, so-called performing notes issued after the nation's 2001 default were "mainly in positive territory, up on average by half a percentage point," said fixed income analyst Javier Salvucci of local Silver Cloud Advisors.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the market for defaulted debt has disappeared with the end of the debt swap offering period, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Salvucci described the day's session as "calm," with many investors apparently still waiting for official debt swap results later this week.  \par \par \uc2 There is also some speculation that the performing notes, especially peso-denominated bonds, will loose ground on arbitrage actions once new bonds are issued in April, Salvucci said.  \par \par \uc2 In late afternoon trading, the dollar-denominated Boden 2012 was quoted up to ARS261 from ARS260.6 on Friday, while the Boden 2008, a peso note, was at ARS113.13, down from ARS114.8.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson and Vanessa Nichols, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 28-02-05 2011GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050228e12s00151\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
