\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Argentina  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buys Dlrs To Weaken Peso; Debt Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2005\par 21:05\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Feb 10, 2005 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 Late session \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday managed to weaken the peso, a day after it hit its strongest point against the dollar since May. Meanwhile, local bonds continued to rally in reaction to news that the yield on 10-year U.S. Treasurys ended below 4% for the first time in three months Wednesday. The peso closed the day at ARS2.91375 against the dollar, slightly weaker than Wednesday's ARS2.90875. Heavier than usual volume suggested that investors may be returning to the otherwise illiquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dominated by cereal exporters selling dollar earnings and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trader Fernando Santiago Izzo said. "If it weren't for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Banco de la Nacion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso would be much stronger," said Izzo, of local brokerage ABC Mercado de Cambio. Constrained by tighter monetary policy goals for the first quarter, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has significantly reduced its dollar buying this year. Observers believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trying to keep the exchange rate near ARS3 to the dollar in a bid maintain Argentine export competitiveness. Since mid-January, peso traders have also noticed increased dollar buying by state-owned Banco de la Nacion, which is less restricted than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts also believe that Banco de la Nacion dollar buying is picking up in preparation for bondholder payments expected in the coming months. Both the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Banco de la Nacion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, with the latter buying the bulk of the dollars to push back the peso, Izzo said. He speculated that the bank has set ARS2.90 as the peso's new ceiling against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 02-10-05 1501ET  \par \par \uc2 Copyright 2004 Dow Jones. All rights reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050210e12a0050q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
