\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buys Dlrs To Weaken Peso; Debt Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2005\par 21:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Late session \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday managed to weaken the peso, a day after it hit its strongest point against the dollar since May.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, local bonds continued to rally in reaction to news that the yield on 10-year U.S. Treasurys ended below 4% for the first time in three months Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed the day at ARS2.91375 against the dollar, slightly weaker than Wednesday's ARS2.90875.  \par \par \uc2 Heavier than usual volume suggested that investors may be returning to the otherwise illiquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dominated by cereal exporters selling dollar earnings and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trader Fernando Santiago Izzo said.  \par \par \uc2 "If it weren't for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Banco de la Nacion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso would be much stronger," said Izzo, of local brokerage ABC Mercado de Cambio.  \par \par \uc2 Constrained by tighter monetary policy goals for the first quarter, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has significantly reduced its dollar buying this year. Observers believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trying to keep the exchange rate near ARS3 to the dollar in a bid maintain Argentine export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 Since mid-January, peso traders have also noticed increased dollar buying by state-owned Banco de la Nacion, which is less restricted than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts also believe that Banco de la Nacion dollar buying is picking up in preparation for bondholder payments expected in the coming months.  \par \par \uc2 Both the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Banco de la Nacion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, with the latter buying the bulk of the dollars to push back the peso, Izzo said. He speculated that the bank has set ARS2.90 as the peso's new ceiling against the dollar. [ 10-02-05 2001GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, volume was relatively heavy with investor interest in both pre- and post-default bonds, said fixed income analyst Diego Zavaleta with local Besfamille Sociedad de Bolsa.  \par \par \uc2 Zavaleta added that the lower yield on the 10-year U.S. Treasurys has led some investors to reevaluate the terms of Argentina's ongoing sovereign debt swap and start buying more defaulted notes.  \par \par \uc2 Among gainers, the benchmark peso-denominated Boden 2008 was quoted at ARS113.76, compared with ARS113.1 on Wednesday, while the Boden 2012, a dollar-denominated note, was at ARS254.85, up 50 centavos on the day.  \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson and Vanessa Nichols, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com. [ 10-02-05 2019GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050210e12a000vo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
