\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks sink along with foreign markets.   \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2004\par 21:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Nov 19 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks closed down on Friday after markets abroad turned lower on the sharp jump in oil prices, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The MerVal .MERV) index of 11 leading shares ended 0.72 percent lower at 1254.45 after rising nearly 1 percent in the morning. The market is down 2.5 percent so far in November, but is up 17 percent since the beginning of the year.   \par \par \uc2 Trading volume was low at 49.3 million pesos ($16.7 million).   \par \par \uc2 "It was hard to maintain the rise at the beginning of the day because we had an international context of declines in reaction to a new increase in the price of oil," said Hernan Labrone, trader at Fenix Compania Financiera.   \par \par \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia, which accounts for a quarter of the MerVal, ended 1.78 percent lower at 2.21 pesos.   \par \par \uc2 Investors await news on Argentina's debt swap due to begin on Nov. 29 and the beginning of the government's roadshow.   \par \par \uc2 Argentina's Economy Minister has yet to inform when the roadshow will begin, but local media has said it could kick off next Wednesday in Buenos Aires.   \par \par \uc2 Argentina wants to issue $41.8 billion in new debt for the $102.6 billion in debt in default, but it has to convince more than 500,000 private creditors to accept an estimated 70 percent loss on their investments.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso ARSB=) closed unchanged at 2.945/2.95 per dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $47 million to keep the peso from strengthening further.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a daily basis to keep the peso competitive for export purposes.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041119e0bj00e1m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
