\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Peso Continues To Gain Against Dlr; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2004\par 20:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to crank up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, but again failed to restrain the strengthening peso, which marked its fourth day of gains against the sliding dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the debt market saw gains as investors sought out bonds amid tight supply.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at 2.9350 to the dollar, up more than a centavo from ARS2.9525 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $40 million on the open market Wednesday, the largest single-day buy since mid-June. The purchase marks a sizable increase from daily purchases of about $30 million in recent weeks.  \par \par \uc2 Under \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Martin Redrado, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used large dollar purchases to maintain the peso in a tight range of about ARS2.96 to ARS2.98 against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 As a result, the peso now appears cheap in comparison to the euro, and more importantly, the real from neighboring Brazil, as the dollar continues to weaken against these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Daniel Bou-Kahir, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk at local Banco de la Pampa, said that Wednesday's market was filled with peso-buyers, helping fuel the peso's drive upward against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 He also noted that Argentine cereal "exporters are getting ahead on their liquidations," motivated by concerns about the dollar's continued slide.  \par \par \uc2 "The peso strengthening is more speculative than based on concrete news," Bou-Kahir said when asked about a Tuesday announcement by Argentine officials that Chinese companies are interested in investing nearly $20 billion in local projects.  \par \par \uc2 Instead, "exporters are worried about a weakening dollar and covering their positions," Bou-Kahir added.  \par \par \uc2 Along with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Argentina's grain exporters are the largest actors in the illiquid peso market as they repatriate dollar-denominated earnings.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, grain exporters liquidated $63.9 million, a considerable increase from their dollar sales over the past week that hovered around $30 million. Wednesday figures were due in later in the day. [ 17-11-04 1954GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 In the debt market, bonds generally gained as investors sought out local notes.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is very well bid today," said one local bond trader, who described volume as slightly higher than average. "It's hard to find paper. Especially for investors looking to buy in size," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The continued demand for Argentine bonds comes as investors remain generally optimistic about the nation's debt swap offer, slated to open on Nov. 29 and close on Jan. 17.  \par \par \uc2 And the good vibe got a boost late Tuesday - after the local market close - when New York District Court Judge Thomas Griesa turned down a bondholder bid for an injunction on the debt restructure offering.  \par \par \uc2 In afternoon trading, the peso-denominated benchmark Boden 2008 was up to 108.64 from 107.5, while the Pre-8, a peso note, was rising from 145.75 to 146.80.  \par \par \uc2 -By Suzelle Tempero and Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 17-11-04 2036GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041117e0bh000ym\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
