\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina peso ends stable, stocks rise 2.1 pct.  \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2004\par 23:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, April 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso closed unchanged on Tuesday due to strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at stopping the appreciation of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has approached eight-month highs.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended at 2.820/2.825 pesos per dollar, still up 1.5 percent this month and 5.0 percent since the start of the year mainly due to a boom in exports, especially grains.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $45 million on Tuesday to keep the peso steady, similar to Monday's levels but higher than the roughly $30 million daily average earlier this year.  \par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may now have decided to keep the peso trading within a range of between 2.75 pesos and 2.85 pesos, a tacit acceptance that levels of over 2.90 pesos, seen as recently as February, will not return.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, stocks rose 2.09 percent to 1,202.5 points on moderate volume of 48.9 million pesos ($17.3 million) - the first rise after four consecutive sessions of falls as investors made some cautious buys ahead of future stock options that mature on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Among leading blue chips, Grupo Financiero Galicia (GFG.BA) rose 3.91 percent to 2.39 pesos on investor expectations that the stock will rise on Thursday after future stock options have matured.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040413e04d0036q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
