\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Peso Strengthens As Exporters Return To Mkt  \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2003\par 20:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso strengthened modestly Tuesday, as exporters started to return to the market after having been sidelined during a more volatile trading period at the end of last month.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.955 to the dollar in the interbank market, one centavo stronger than its ARS2.965 close on Friday. Monday was a holiday for financial markets in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Traders said it appeared the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with its routine dollar-buying, but this was overwhelmed by dollar supply from the exporters. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly bought $30 million a day in the market over the past two months to help supplement otherwise thin natural demand for the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was active, what we are seeing now is what we expected to see toward the middle of the month, and that is the growth in inflows from exporters," said one trader with an international bank. He said the biggest Argentine exporters, the grain producers, remain somewhat sidelined and that when they start transferring their foreign earnings into local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the upward pressure on the peso will be stronger.  \par \par \uc2 However, the market can be expected to abide by the new trading range it appeared to establish after a big selloff in the peso two weeks ago, he said. Whereas formerly the peso was in a range of ARS2.80 to ARS2.90 to the dollar, it now looks to be trading between ARS2.90 and ARS3.00.  \par \par \uc2 "I would expect to see some (dollar) long positions put on" as the peso approaches ARS2.90 to the dollar, the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Official data later showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  markedly increased its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $40 million for the day. This was a big departure from the standard $30 million level of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for most of the past two months, and one of the biggest daily dollar purchase figures for the year.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed its reference rate at ARS2.9547 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 -By Michael Casey, Dow Jones Newswires; michael.j.casey@dowjones.com; 54-11-4313 1918  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031209dzc9000x6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
