\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Prat Gay Stresses Peso In Free Float Regime  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,100 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2003\par 22:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 PILAR, Argentina (Dow Jones)--In the wake of sharp slide in the peso against the dollar last week that raised speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is targeting a lower level for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Alfonso Prat Gay insisted Tuesday the peso will stay in a free-floating arrangement.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars against the peso in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were entirely driven by monetary policy goals - efforts to boost the monetary base as a stimulative measure - rather than a exchange rate target, Prat Gay said in a speech to a major business conference.  \par \par \uc2 "It must remain absolutely clear that we are in a regime of floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Prat Gay said. He was speaking at the annual conference of Argentina's leading business organization, the Argentine Industrial Union, in Pilar, just outside Buenos Aires.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president said, however, that the free float - adopted in January 2001 after Argentina ended the peso's one-to-one peg to the dollar - didn't preclude \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for pursuing monetary goals. It doesn't mean, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't have an "active monetary policy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Moreover, he sought to play down the continued attention on the peso's value to the dollar, rather than other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The peso's slide to an eight-month low of ARS2.958 to the dollar in the interbank market on Friday had raised talk of a ARS3.00 target, but Prat Gay emphasized that the protection of Argentina's competitiveness should be considered against the multitude of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats.  \par \par \uc2 "A multilateral competitive rate" is important, he said, adding that "we shouldn't tie ourselves to the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 Whereas the peso lost 3.3% against the dollar last week, boosting the competitiveness of Argentine products in the U.S., it has gained even more in competitiveness against the euro, against which the dollar itself has been hitting record lows.  \par \par \uc2 The peso's sharp move last week came as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its policy of buying dollars in the open market. Although traders had expected it to hold back from such purchases once the peso dropped below ARS2.90 to the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to accept dollar offers in a way that led many to conclude it was now deliberately targeting a lower rate.  \par \par \uc2 However, Prat Gay was insistent Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's goal is one of "stability" in the exchange rate and avoiding "volatility" rather than exchange rate targeting.  \par \par \uc2 This is consistent with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official position for much of this year. In the absence of any natural demand for dollars while many Argentine borrowers are still not servicing defaulted foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has insisted on filling that gap to prevent disorderly movements as export-driven peso demand flows in unabated.  \par \par \uc2 "This obsession with confusing exchange rate policy with monetary policy or the rate of exchange with the price of the dollar doesn't have to exist," Prat Gay said Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "We all know that just as we tied ourselves to the dollar in the 1990s while the dollar was rising against the rest of the world's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the only thing we achieved was to (import) deflation," he said. "To tie ourselves to the dollar at this moment when it is falling would be to import inflation."  \par \par \uc2 Prat Gay named no individuals in his speech, but his position stands in contrast to views widely believed to be held by certain officials within the government of President Nestor Kirchner. These people say Argentina should strive to keep the peso below ARS3.00 to the dollar, a level consistently cited by exporters and industrialists.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, in comments that got him in hot water with the presidential office, Prat Gay called Kirchner's stated interest in attaining that rate "an enormous mistake."  \par \par \uc2 There may also be a difference of opinion arising with Economy Minister Roberto Lavagna. Apparently differing from Prat Gay's interpretation of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a monetary policy tool rather than an exchange rate-targeting tool, Lavagna was quoted by local media earlier Tuesday as saying that "managing the exchange rate is central for avoiding internal and external deficits."  \par \par \uc2 Lavagna may get a chance to respond to Prat Gay when he speaks midday Wednesday at the same conference.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Prat Gay also addressed another issue that seems to have aroused differences of opinion with the Economy Minister, that of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plan to introduce an inflation-targeting system. Last week, Lavagna seemed lukewarm to this idea - which Prat Gay maintains will be a central objective next year - when he warned against "falling in love with these policy tools."  \par \par \uc2 In his speech Tuesday, Prat-Gay appeared to play down the notion that the inflation-targeting regime would be a rigid system and that there would be flexibility in the way it is managed.  \par \par \uc2 He said it is important to "move rapidly to an inflation-targeting regime," but added there "doesn't have to be an obsession with the price index, nor is it a fashion."  \par \par \uc2 "It is something that any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to do when it must defend the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Prat Gay said, in reference to the oft-cited third article of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's charter that makes defending the peso's purchasing power its central objective.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, Prat Gay also called on the government to quickly move to scrap the "distortive" tax it imposes on financial transactions.  \par \par \uc2 "We hope it will be one of the first on the list at the moment of thinking about reducing taxes," he said, noting the huge costs that the so-called checking tax imposes on companies wanting to use the financial system.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, he also claimed that the long-awaited revival of credit is starting within the embattled financial sector, noting that private sector loans have grown 9% in four months. "I believe we have reason to be optimistic about the financial system recovering" from last year's financial crisis, Prat Gay said.  \par \par \uc2 He also emphasized measures taken to create protections against volatility now that the peso has been devalued and that the economy has been "pesified." Among these, he said, were recent measures to promote a peso futures market and a plan to create more cooperation with six different regional central banks. He did not elaborate on this latter idea.  \par \par \uc2 -By Michael Casey and Laurence Norman, Dow Jones Newswires; michael.j.casey@dowjones.com; 54-11-4313 1918  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031202dzc200106\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
