\par\par \b \uc2  Argentina Peso Continues Recovery, As Exporters Weigh In \b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2003\par 20:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES -(Dow Jones)- Argentina's peso continued its rebound Tuesday as a strong inflow of dollars from exporters boosted the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 1750 GMT, the peso was trading at ARS2.885 to the dollar, four centavos stronger than its close of ARS2.925 on the local market Monday. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had hit ARS2.975 on Monday - its weakest levels in weeks. \par \par \uc2  The peso fell back sharply in the second half of last week, amid political uncertainty, inviting the re-entrance of exporters into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when that fall bottomed out late Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The principal reason of the peso's rise is exporter activity," said Carlos Lizer, trader at local stockbrokers Puente Hermanos. "The price near ARS3.00 was good for exporters to sell their dollars." \par \par \uc2  Traders said an increase in dollars repatriated by agricultural exporters was the main reason behind the greater supply of dollars. On Monday, the last day for which data was available, grain traders sold $81.7 million in foreign earnings to the local market. This was a marked increase from the appromixately $50 million they sold at the end of last week. Cereal exporters have represented around one-third of all Argentine exports in recent months. \par \par \uc2  Corrected May 20, 2003 17:18 ET (21:18 GMT) \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the peso seemed to ignore the unveiling of the new cabinet by incoming President Nestor Kirchner on Tuesday morning. Kirchner threw few surprises in his announcement, though the appointment of left-leaning intellectual Rafael Bielsa in the Foreign Ministry raised a few eyebrows. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said there was nothing that would either trouble or inspire the markets and therefore the peso was not budged. \par \par \uc2  "There was no nasty surprises, it was in line with what was expected," said Rafael Ber, senior analyst at local consultancy Argentine Research. \par \par \uc2  The lack of reaction to the Kirchner cabinet contrasted with the market's reaction to last week's political noise, when Carlos Menem's withdrawal from the presidential race and Kirchner's subsequent victory sparked the peso's sell-off. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, no figures were yet available for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, though analysts said they thought the monetary body was continuing to keep a low profile in the market. \par \par \uc2  -By Wailin Wong, Dow Jones Newswires; argentina@dowjones.com; 54-11-4314 2272 \par \par \uc2  At 1750 GMT, the peso was trading at ARS2.885 to the dollar, four centavos stronger than its close of ARS2.925 on the local market Monday. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had hit ARS2.975 on Monday - its weakest levels in weeks. \par \par \uc2  (In an item that ran around 1840 GMT (2:40 p.m. EDT), the level was incorrectly reported.) \par \par \uc2  Later, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it had bought some $85.7 million in a bid to stem the peso's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  The bank had slashed back its activity in recent days, as the peso's decline relieved the pressure on the monetary body to step in. But with the supply of U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again overwhelming the demand for dollars, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to let the peso jump or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Wailin Wong and Laurence Norman, Dow Jones Newswires; \b \highlight22\uc2 argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 @dowjones.com; 54-11-4314 2272 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030520dz5k0014q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
