\par\par \b \uc2  Argentina stocks end up, peso flat on Cenbank moves. \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2002\par 22:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Sept 20 (Reuters) - Argentine \par \par \uc2  shares closed a shade higher on Friday after six sessions of \par \par \uc2  declines and the peso leveled out following recent weakness due \par \par \uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2      Traders said they feared \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inability to reach an \par \par \uc2  aid deal with the International Monetary Fund despite months of \par \par \uc2  tough negotiations could force the government to default on its \par \par \uc2  debts with the IMF and other multilateral lenders like the \par \par \uc2  World Bank. \par \par \uc2      A multilateral default would cut off Argentina's only \par \par \uc2  source of financing after stopping payment on most of its $104 \par \par \uc2  billion debt in January and further isolate the country just as \par \par \uc2  a four-year recession shows signs of leveling off. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso         ended virtually unchanged at 3.67/3.68 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar in large-scale transactions in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market compared with Thursday's close of 3.67/3.69.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The peso fell Thursday with people buying dollars but\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and mandatory exporter sales of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars are keeping the peso stable," a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso has been relatively stable for the last two months\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rules requiring buyers of more than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $100,000 in dollars to have prior authorization have helped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso is about 72 percent weaker since January's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par devaluation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Buenos Aires Stock Exchange's benchmark MerVal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par share index edged 0.09 percent higher to 376.79 points on very\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par thin turnover of 22 million pesos ($6 million). Overall, 23\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par issues advanced, 14 fell and six were unchanged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Financial holding Grupo Financiero Galicia gained\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slightly to 0.273 peso and was the most heavily traded share of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the session while energy group Perez Companc closed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unchanged at 1.84 pesos.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The MerVal is up about 28 percent so far this year as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Argentines have sought equities as a hedge against the peso's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par devaluation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020920dy9k01378\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
