\par\par \b \uc2  Argentine stocks dip, peso off despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2002\par 19:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      BUENOS AIRES, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , June 24 (Reuters) - Argentine \par \par \uc2  stocks fell on Monday afternoon, while the peso weakened \par \par \uc2  despite heavy buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said, citing \par \par \uc2  mounting fears over the stubborn recession afflicting Latin \par \par \uc2  America's third largest economy, \par \par \uc2      Argentina's leading MerVal .MERV) share index lost 1.76 \par \par \uc2  percent to 307 points in below-average volume of 10.8 million \par \par \uc2  pesos. The MerVal is down 5 percent since Jan. 2 and off 3 \par \par \uc2  percent in June as investors fear the long recession could \par \par \uc2  leave Argentine companies unable to pay their debts. \par \par \uc2      Overall, 15 shares declined, five shares advanced and five \par \par \uc2  traded unchanged. \par \par \uc2      Grupo Financiero Galicia was the most heavily traded stock, \par \par \uc2  unchanged at 0.19 pesos after last week's gain of 45 percent on \par \par \uc2  rumors it might sell its main unit, Argentina's largest private \par \par \uc2  bank Banco Galicia. \par \par \uc2  Energy group Perez Companc lost 3.05 percent to 1.91 pesos \par \par \uc2  after a local bank said it had rejected a $101 million debt \par \par \uc2  payment originally due in U.S. dollars made instead with 104.57 \par \par \uc2  million pesos ($28 million). \par \par \uc2  The peso fell 1.6 percent to 3.80/3.81 per dollar in \par \par \uc2  large-scale transactions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market ARSB=) \par \par \uc2  compared with Friday's close of 3.73/3.75. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the peso's fall came despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling by midday an \par \par \uc2  unusually heavy $40 million out of U.S. dollar reserves that \par \par \uc2  have dwindled by nearly 50 percent this year. \par \par \uc2  "We're looking at a complicated week because Argentina is \par \par \uc2  trying to reach a deal with the IMF, but also there are some \par \par \uc2  complications around the region that are putting a worrying \par \par \uc2  pressure on business," said a banking analyst. \par \par \uc2  Economy Minister Roberto Lavagna is slated to travel to \par \par \uc2  Washington this week to try to end months of stalemate and \par \par \uc2  reach an aid deal with the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  Many analysts fear, however, that Argentina will not be \par \par \uc2  able to make spending cuts or keep monetary policy as tight as \par \par \uc2  the IMF demands in return for aid. \par \par \uc2  Troubles in neighboring powerhouse Brazil have also hurt \par \par \uc2  Argentina. Brazil's real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hit all-time lows on debt \par \par \uc2  and pre-election jitters. \par \par \uc2  Argentina's peso is about 73 percent weaker since January's \par \par \uc2  devaluation, which came amid a devastating four-year recession \par \par \uc2  that has left the entire financial system near collapse and \par \par \uc2  sparked fears of hyperinflation. \par \par \uc2  Outgoing \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Mario Blejer said in comments \par \par \uc2  published on Monday he saw the peso's level stronger than 4.0 \par \par \uc2  per dollar by the end of 2002 and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  would continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. 