\par\par \b \uc2  Argentina Ctrl Bank -2: `We'll Make Dollar Fall': Duhalde \b0\par\par\uc2 627 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 18:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Executives at local banks and officers of the Argentine Banking Association were still evaluating the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  order and weren't immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  In a Friday interview with Radio America and without mentioning specific actions, President Eduardo Duhalde said "We'll make the dollar fall." \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent between $100 million and $150 million buying pesos in an effort to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Earlier in the week, after Duhalde made similar comments, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent an estimated $80 million to buy pesos. \par \par \uc2  Duhalde and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Mario Blejer both said the government will use all resources available to it to keep the dollar at about ARS1.65. \par \par \uc2  Critics on Wall Street and in Argentina oppose the government's spending of scarce hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to protect an overvalued peso while local companies can't get credit to remain operating, and bondholders can't get repaid for the sovereign debt they own. \par \par \uc2  On Jan. 6, Argentina devalued the peso from its 11-year, 1-to-1 peg with the dollar by an initial 29%. The Duhalde administration began to float the peso against the greenback on Feb. 11, several months ahead of schedule. \par \par \uc2  About $400 million a day trades in Argentina's infant \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to the latest estimates of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Club of Argentina. \par \par \uc2  "We're taking our first steps. Now all volume is related to (the needs of importers and exporters). "We haven't begun the speculative market," said Jose Alfredo Nogueira, of the ABC Mercado de Cambios, a former banker. \par \par \uc2  By some calculations, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent between $700 million and $900 million to slow the slide in the peso. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refuses to comment on what it spends each day in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  To some analysts, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is confused and misguided. \par \par \uc2  "In \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many politicians and even some economists don't understand the first thing about (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) markets," Nogueira said. \par \par \uc2  The government's main goal is to prevent the four-digit annual hyperinflation of the late 1980s that forced Argentina in 1991 to peg its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the U.S. dollar at a rate of 1-to-1. \par \par \uc2  Argentina is struggling to escape a four-year recession that has forced urban unemployment past 20% and pushed tens of thousands of middle-class families into poverty. \par \par \uc2  The Duhalde administration hopes that if it can keep a lid on consumer prices, it can prevent the street protests and supermarket looting that forced the Dec. 20 resignation of former President Fernando de la Rua. \par \par \uc2  -By Tim Loughran, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4313-1918; tim.loughran@dowjones.com. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued an update of Rule 3511 that tightened some, and loosened other, restrictions on dollar holdings. \par \par \uc2  On the one hand, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that banks' new General Exchange Position as defined by Rule 3511 would include the sum of all types of cash and liquid investments held in any form overseas. \par \par \uc2  Also, any Argentine bank that fails to report its dollar holdings to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of each day, by 2300 GMT, will not be able to participate in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amended Rule 3511 to say that all local banks are entitled to have at least $1 million in dollar holdings each day, easing the original terms set Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that some smaller banks, if forced to abide by Rule 3511's original 5% threshold, might not be able to serve their customers properly. \par \par \uc2  -By Tim Loughran, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4313-1918; tim.loughran@dowjones.com. \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020315dy3f0010a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
