\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2 's Peso Ends Weaker Despite Heavy  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 21:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso (ARS) closed slightly weaker Thursday, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most significant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to float in early January. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $120 million to prop up the ever-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Commercial banks quoted the peso closing at a midrate of  around ARS2.39/dollar for interbank transactions. On Wednesday the peso closed at ARS2.36/dollar for such transactions. \par \par \uc2  Other traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold as much as $150 million Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday around ARS2.32 to ARS2.38. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday was the highest level of dollar sales since the peso began floating at the beginning of the year. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't keep the price of the peso from falling, traders noted. "It's the forces of the market versus the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is losing for now, one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  blew through $18 million in about one minute in early trading, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around ARS2.32 and ARS2.34. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a matter of policy doesn't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The peso, which for 11 years was pegged 1:1 to the U.S. dollar, began to float freely in early January after the government devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Government and monetary officials, from President Eduardo Duhalde to \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Mario Blejer, have vowed to use the country's hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to prop up the peso. Officials have said the government would like to see the peso trading at ARS1.60/dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses in downtown Buenos Aires were selling dollars to the public around ARS2.42 and buying greenbacks for around ARS2.28. \par \par \uc2  -By Dawn Weiner, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; argentina@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020314dy3e0019u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
